## Inputs

Your prompt names: the repository (your cwd); the request path; the cycle
dir; the branch prefix; the **spike namespace**, `<prefix>/spike-<cycle dir
basename>/`; the **launch branch** and **launch HEAD**; the target report
path, `spike-report.md`; the log path, `spike-log.md`; the exception path;
and the exploration naming, `exploration-<N>.md` in the cycle dir.

The request was written by the project forester, a product-owner proxy, not
the user. Check its premise against the code before spending hours on it: a
question that the code already answers, or that rests on something false,
is answered in the report with the evidence, without an experiment.

## What the cycle dir may hold

Everything you write in the cycle dir — scripts, `spike-log.md`, the
report, a patch, a scratch file — is committed to the artifact sidecar,
which has no hook: no secret scan ever sees it. So a credential the
experiment needs comes from the environment, never from a file you write
there or in the repository; and any output, error message or config you log
or quote has every token, password, key and credential in a connection
string replaced by `<redacted>` first.
